WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.030
King Henry was extremely angry.

2
00:00:05.031 --> 00:00:10.674
He'd promised Queen Eleanor that her three archers could go free for forty days.

3
00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:14.261
But the archers turned out to be Robin Hood and his men!

4
00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:20.447
When the king returned to his castle, he sat in silence, furiously biting his lip.

5
00:00:20.448 --> 00:00:23.424
The Bishop of Hereford sat with him.

6
00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:27.438
So did a good, honest knight named Sir Lee.

7
00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:29.747
Finally the bishop spoke up.

8
00:00:29.748 --> 00:00:33.817
"Your Majesty, I know you want to keep your promise to the queen.

9
00:00:33.818 --> 00:00:36.771
But Robin Hood is right here in London.

10
00:00:36.772 --> 00:00:39.327
He's the greatest villain in England.

11
00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:41.919
It's a shame to let him get away."

12
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.840
The king lifted his eyes and looked glumly at the bishop.

13
00:00:45.841 --> 00:00:49.669
"I can't break my word to my wife.

14
00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:55.280
When forty days have passed, we'll go after Robin Hood."

15
00:00:55.281 --> 00:00:58.727
The Bishop of Hereford hated Robin and his men.

16
00:00:58.728 --> 00:01:02.460
He spoke carefully, in a soft, smooth voice.

17
00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:07.804
"Once Robin returns to Sherwood Forest, you'll never find him, Your Majesty.

18
00:01:07.805 --> 00:01:11.741
He knows that area far better than you do."

19
00:01:11.742 --> 00:01:15.128
The king tapped his fingers on the table in front of him.

20
00:01:15.129 --> 00:01:21.217
"But what about my promise? Didn't you hear me give her my word?"

21
00:01:21.218 --> 00:01:23.250
The bishop cleared his throat.

22
00:01:23.251 --> 00:01:27.146
"You of course know your wife best, Your Majesty.

23
00:01:27.147 --> 00:01:32.806
But I'm sure that the queen has forgotten all about Robin Hood by now."

24
00:01:32.807 --> 00:01:38.763
He laughed loudly. "Women are so easily distracted."

25
00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:40.755
The king thought about that.

26
00:01:40.756 --> 00:01:42.972
Then he finally made up his mind.

27
00:01:42.973 --> 00:01:48.358
"Sir Lee! Take six men and seize Robin at the archery field.

28
00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:52.161
Throw him and his two men in prison!"

29
00:01:52.162 --> 00:01:55.247
Sir Lee was a gentle and noble knight.

30
00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:59.255
He was upset to hear the king breaking his word to his wife.

31
00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:03.428
But he couldn't say anything; he was only the king's servant.

32
00:02:03.429 --> 00:02:06.990
"Yes, Your Majesty," Sir Lee mumbled.

33
00:02:06.991 --> 00:02:09.732
He bowed to the king and left the room.

34
00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:13.532
Sir Lee had made up his mind about something too.

35
00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:18.863
Before rounding up the men, he found the queen and told her what had happened.

36
00:02:18.864 --> 00:02:21.619
"You must warn Robin!" he said.

37
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.373
"Why are you so worried about an outlaw?" asked Queen Eleanor.

38
00:02:26.374 --> 00:02:29.960
"I don't care about Robin," Sir Lee explained.

39
00:02:29.961 --> 00:02:36.561
"I'm upset that the king is breaking his promise to you!"

40
00:02:36.562 --> 00:02:41.691
"I've already warned Robin that the king is angry," said the queen.

41
00:02:41.692 --> 00:02:48.084
"But now I must send another warning. Thank you, Sir Lee."

42
00:02:48.085 --> 00:02:53.641
Meanwhile Robin and his men had already left London.

43
00:02:53.642 --> 00:02:57.325
It was almost dark when Robin pointed to an inn.

44
00:02:57.326 --> 00:02:59.780
"There's a place we can spend the night."

45
00:02:59.781 --> 00:03:04.501
"And get something to eat," said Little John, who was always hungry.

46
00:03:04.502 --> 00:03:07.569
Will Scarlet looked around uneasily.

47
00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:11.601
"I wish we were farther away from London," he murmured.

48
00:03:11.602 --> 00:03:15.421
"I'm sure the king will send men after us."

49
00:03:15.422 --> 00:03:18.904
"Don't worry. We'll be safe here," said Robin.

50
00:03:18.905 --> 00:03:22.037
Will still looked uneasy but he shrugged.

51
00:03:22.038 --> 00:03:23.939
"Whatever you say, Robin."

52
00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.206
The three men went into the inn.

53
00:03:26.207 --> 00:03:29.117
The innkeeper served them a fine meal.

54
00:03:29.118 --> 00:03:33.798
Then, while they were busy eating, he approached Robin again.

55
00:03:33.799 --> 00:03:39.336
"There's a young man outside who wants to speak to you," said the innkeeper.

56
00:03:39.337 --> 00:03:42.213
"He says he's the queen's page."

57
00:03:42.214 --> 00:03:45.391
Robin got up from the table and went outside.

58
00:03:45.392 --> 00:03:49.339
Little John and Will looked at each other nervously.

59
00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:54.248
Outside, the queen's page sat on his horse in the white moonlight.

60
00:03:54.249 --> 00:03:57.662
"The queen sent me to warn you," said the page.

61
00:03:57.663 --> 00:04:02.392
"The Bishop of Hereford has encouraged the king to break his promise.

62
00:04:02.393 --> 00:04:06.827
King Henry sent Sir Lee to arrest you at the archery field.

63
00:04:06.828 --> 00:04:12.953
But you'd already left. More than a thousand men are after you right now!"

64
00:04:12.954 --> 00:04:17.143
"This is the second time the queen has saved me," said Robin.

65
00:04:17.144 --> 00:04:19.675
"Please thank her for this new warning."

66
00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:22.213
"Hurry!" the page urged him.

67
00:04:22.214 --> 00:04:25.310
"Two bands of horsemen are right behind me!"

68
00:04:25.311 --> 00:04:30.303
"I'll tell the innkeeper we're going to Saint Albans," said Robin quickly.

69
00:04:30.304 --> 00:04:33.638
"But we won't go anywhere near that town."

70
00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:36.895
Robin went inside and spoke to the innkeeper.

71
00:04:36.896 --> 00:04:39.281
"We won't be spending the night after all.

72
00:04:39.282 --> 00:04:45.848
We're heading to Saint Albans. Let's go, men!"

73
00:04:45.849 --> 00:04:49.889
Back on the road, Robin explained what was happening.

74
00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.315
"We should split up," said Will Scarlet.

75
00:04:52.316 --> 00:04:55.362
"I'll go with Little John, and you travel alone, Robin."

76
00:04:55.363 --> 00:04:58.329
"We'll head in different directions," said Robin.

77
00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.192
"If we're caught, we won't be caught together."

78
00:05:01.193 --> 00:05:06.725
"Right!" said Will. "See you at home!"

79
00:05:06.726 --> 00:05:11.220
After eight days Will and Little John reached Sherwood Forest.

80
00:05:11.221 --> 00:05:14.011
Everyone rejoiced to see them.

81
00:05:14.012 --> 00:05:20.325
"Sorry it took us so long," said Little John. "Where's Robin?"

82
00:05:20.326 --> 00:05:26.313
"Robin?" said one of the men. "We thought he was with you."

